      {"level": "integration", "code": ["\\bprovideHttpClient\\s*\\(\\s*\\)"], "unless": ["\\bprovideHttpClientTesting\\s*\\(|\\bHttpClientTestingModule\\b|\\bHttpTestingController\\b"]}
    ]
  },
  "caseMatrix": {
    "$comment": "Fallmatrix (docs/05-analyse.md, 5e). Columns of a parameter table (@ValueSource/@CsvSource method parameters, it.each callback parameters / object keys / template header, Go struct fields) are 'expected' when their name matches one of expectedNames (regexes, Java syntax, searched in the name) or when the name is used only inside assertions of the test body; else 'input'. nameFields: Go struct fields that name a case (t.Run(tt.name, …)); their value becomes the row name instead of a column. A rules file without this section, or without one of its keys, uses the built-in value for that key.",
    "expectedNames": [
      "(?i)^expect(ed)?\\w*$",
      "(?i)^exp$",
      "(?i)^want(ed)?\\w*$",
      "(?i)^(result|outcome|output|out|answer)\\w*$",
      "(?i)^(http)?status(code)?$",
      "(?i)^(message|msg|error|err|errorMessage|errMsg)s?$",
      "(?i)^(is)?(valid|ok|success|accepted|allowed)$",
      "(?i)^response\\w*$",
      "(?i)^should\\w*$"
    ],
    "nameFields": [
      "(?i)^(name|desc|description|title|scenario|testName|caseName)$"
    ]
  },
  "relatedTests": {
    "$comment": "Bestehende Tests (docs/05-analyse.md, 5f). For every changed source file existing, unchanged test files of the repository are loaded and linked to the changed code: named after it (X.spec.ts, XTest.java, XTests.java, XIT.java, x_test.go, ...) in the mirrored test directory or next to it ('mirror'), else the nearest file of that name elsewhere ('name'), plus test files in the mirrored directory whose name starts with it (PlayerResourceSecurityTest, 'prefix'). limit: at most this many files per pull request (mirror before name before prefix, then by path). mirrors: the first occurrence of 'from' (whole path segments) in the directory of a changed file is replaced by 'to' to get its test directory; the directory itself always counts. A rules file without this section, or without one of its keys, uses the built-in value for that key.",
    "limit": 30,
    "mirrors": [
      {"from": "src/main/", "to": "src/test/"},
      {"from": "main/", "to": "test/"},
      {"from": "src/", "to": "test/"},
      {"from": "src/", "to": "tests/"},
      {"from": "lib/", "to": "test/"}
    ]
  }
